+# HIL Integration Playbook — Industrial Robot (PoC)
+
+Target platform: ROS2-enabled industrial manipulator / mobile base (example vendor: Generic-Industrial-X)
+
+Precautions (MUST READ)
+- Never connect live actuators until E-STOP and watchdog are verified.
+- Use VLAN/isolation for HIL network; separate from corporate LAN.
+- Require physical safety operator present for first runs.
+
+Prerequisites
+- ROS2 Foxy or Humble runtime on HIL host.
+- E-STOP stub in place (ops/robotics/estop/estop_stub.py) or vendor E-STOP hardware.
+- Evidence S3 bucket credentials and operator account.
+
+Steps
+1) Setup environment
+   - Provision HIL host, install ROS2, and ensure time sync (chrony/ntp).
+2) Connect sensors in read-only mode and verify telemetry channels.
+3) Launch E-STOP server and verify it can assert emergency stop.
+4) Run a dry simulation (PyBullet) of scenario, generate trace and upload to evidence bucket.
+5) Run HIL scenario in incremental stages:
+   - Stage A: sensors only (no actuation)
+   - Stage B: actuation with safety limits (reduced velocity)
+   - Stage C: normal velocity with operator supervision
+6) Collect logs, cosign bundles, upload to evidence S3: hil/logs/, sim2real/traces/
+
+E-STOP binding example
+- Vendor exposes HTTP API: POST /api/estop -> engages, POST /api/reset -> clears
+- Use ops/robotics/estop/estop_stub.py in lab for PoC; in production connect to vendor API and ensure hardware interlocks.
+
+Verification & acceptance
+- All safety checks must pass; no unexpected actuator commands recorded.
+- Cosign-signed evidence bundle created for the scenario.
